The chosen weights keep the correct signs for stabilising feedback (negative on cart position and velocity, positive on pole angle and angular velocity) while increasing the magnitudes of the position gain (w0), angle gain (w1) and angular‑velocity gain (w3) to provide stronger corrective forces. The cart‑velocity gain w2 is also made more negative to damp motion faster. No bias term is added (b=0) to avoid a systematic drift. This combination is a modest step away from the best‑performing policies (which suffered from position drift due to too‑small w0) and should reduce drift and improve episode length, moving toward the target reward.
